Renesas FSP UART receive callback not firing in half-duplex RS-485 communication

I am developing firmware in e² studio using Renesas FSP. My goal is to establish half-duplex RS-485 communication between a Renesas MCU with RS485 and a PC using a RS485 - USB DTech adapter.

Hardware and configuration

Renesas MCU

IDE: e² studio

Driver: Renesas FSP SCI UART

Baud rate: 115200, 8-N-1

RS-485 transceiver: [Add model]

UART TXD: P109

UART RXD: P110

DE GPIO: P200

/RE GPIO: P206

The PC and MCU share the RS-485 A/B differential lines. I am manually controlling DE and /RE using GPIO pins.

Expected behavior

The MCU initializes the UART and enters receive mode.

I type Z in the PC terminal.

The MCU receives the character through R_SCI_UART_Read().

The firmware detects Z and transmits z through the same A/B lines.

The MCU returns to receive mode and waits for the next command.

Direction-control logic

void rs485_receive_mode(void)
{
    R_IOPORT_PinWrite(&g_ioport_ctrl,
                      BSP_IO_PORT_02_PIN_00,
                      BSP_IO_LEVEL_LOW);  // DE LOW

    R_IOPORT_PinWrite(&g_ioport_ctrl,
                      BSP_IO_PORT_02_PIN_06,
                      BSP_IO_LEVEL_LOW);  // /RE LOW
}

void rs485_transmit_mode(void)
{
    R_IOPORT_PinWrite(&g_ioport_ctrl,
                      BSP_IO_PORT_02_PIN_06,
                      BSP_IO_LEVEL_HIGH); // /RE HIGH

    R_IOPORT_PinWrite(&g_ioport_ctrl,
                      BSP_IO_PORT_02_PIN_00,
                      BSP_IO_LEVEL_HIGH); // DE HIGH
}

UART callback

volatile bool rx_done = false;
volatile bool tx_done = false;
volatile bool rx_error = false;

void uart_callback(uart_callback_args_t *p_args)
{
    switch (p_args->event)
    {
        case UART_EVENT_RX_COMPLETE:
            rx_done = true;
            break;

        case UART_EVENT_TX_COMPLETE:
            tx_done = true;
            break;

        case UART_EVENT_ERR_FRAMING:
        case UART_EVENT_ERR_PARITY:
        case UART_EVENT_ERR_OVERFLOW:
        case UART_EVENT_BREAK_DETECT:
            rx_error = true;
            rx_done = true;
            break;

        default:
            break;
    }
}

Receive logic

char c;

while (1)
{
    rs485_receive_mode();

    rx_done = false;
    rx_error = false;

    err = R_SCI_UART_Read(&g_uart0_ctrl,
                          (uint8_t *)&c,
                          1U);

    if (err != FSP_SUCCESS)
    {
        continue;
    }

    uint32_t timeout_ms = 3000U;

    while (!rx_done && timeout_ms > 0U)
    {
        R_BSP_SoftwareDelay(1U, BSP_DELAY_UNITS_MILLISECONDS);
        timeout_ms--;
    }

    if (!rx_done)
    {
        // Receive timeout
        continue;
    }

    if (rx_error)
    {
        rx_error = false;
        continue;
    }

    if (c == 'Z' || c == 'z')
    {
        uint8_t response = 'z';

        rs485_transmit_mode();

        // UART transmission and TX-completion handling
        // are implemented in my rs485_write() function.
        rs485_write(&response, 1U);
    }
}

Problem

The UART initialization succeeds, and the MCU can transmit data to the PC. However, when I type a character in the PC terminal, the receive-completion flag does not appear to be set reliably, and the firmware times out waiting for UART_EVENT_RX_COMPLETE.

I have configured the FSP UART callback and assigned the UART TX/RX pins. I am also manually controlling DE and /RE. I want to use manual GPIO direction control rather than automatic RS-485 DE control.

Questions

Is this the correct sequence for R_SCI_UART_Read() and manual RS-485 direction control in Renesas FSP?

Are there any FSP UART configuration or interrupt settings that could prevent UART_EVENT_RX_COMPLETE from firing?

What is the recommended way to manage TX completion and DE timing before returning to receive mode?

How should I diagnose whether the issue is in the UART configuration, transceiver direction control, or physical A/B connection?

I would appreciate a working example or guidance specific to Renesas FSP and half-duplex RS-485 communication.

